{# Modern <source> of a <picture> over an ingested blob.

   MinIO stores images content-addressed with a sibling WebP next to the PNG, so
   the modern candidate is DERIVED from the original path, never carried in the
   payload. Deriving it for anything but a .png would point the browser at a file
   that was never written (silent 404 inside the <picture>) — hence the guard,
   which lives here once instead of in every call site.

   Param: src — browser-ready URL of the original, leading slash included. #}
{%- if src ends with '.png' -%}
    <source srcset="{{ src|replace({'.png': '.webp'}) }}" type="image/webp">
{%- endif -%}
